{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/stock-investing-one-company-or-an-index-fund/audio/main-7abb3bbfa600.mp3","durationSec":301.32,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.88,"text":"A share is one unit of ownership in a company."},{"start":3.72,"end":7.6,"text":"When a company sells shares on a stock exchange, anyone can buy them."},{"start":8.06,"end":13.98,"text":"If the company has one million shares and you buy one thousand, you own 0.1 percent of the business."},{"start":14.82,"end":19.76,"text":"Toyota, for example, has hundreds of millions of shares traded on the Tokyo Stock Exchange."},{"start":20.5,"end":25.68,"text":"Owning Toyota shares means you own a tiny fraction of its factories, vehicles, and future earnings."},{"start":25.68,"end":33.42,"text":"Microsoft has done the same on the Nasdaq exchange in the USA, giving millions of people a stake in its software and cloud services."},{"start":34.74,"end":38.16,"text":"Stock investing fundamentals start with business revenue and profit."},{"start":38.16,"end":43.26,"text":"Revenue is the total money a company receives from selling products or services."},{"start":43.26,"end":46.98,"text":"Profit is what remains after paying all costs."},{"start":47.6,"end":52.16,"text":"A company can have high revenue but low profit when its costs are also high."},{"start":52.68,"end":62.76,"text":"Microsoft reported $281.7 billion in revenue and $101.8 billion in net income for the year ended June 30, 2025."},{"start":64.04,"end":73.42,"text":"ASML, a Dutch maker of chip-making machines, reported €32.7 billion in net sales and €9.6 billion in net income for 2025."},{"start":74.64,"end":79.96,"text":"These numbers describe business performance, but they do not show whether a share price is low or high."},{"start":81,"end":83.82,"text":"Valuation is the market's judgment of what a company is worth."},{"start":84.66,"end":88.98,"text":"Investors compare price with measures such as profit, but future results are uncertain."},{"start":88.98,"end":91.94,"text":"Companies often borrow money to expand."},{"start":92.72,"end":94.14,"text":"This borrowing is called debt."},{"start":94.92,"end":97.76,"text":"Debt is not always bad because it can fund useful growth."},{"start":98.32,"end":102.02,"text":"However, a company must make interest payments and later repay the debt."},{"start":102.02,"end":104.92,"text":"Those payments reduce the money available to shareholders."},{"start":105.94,"end":109.46,"text":"If the business becomes weak, heavy debt can make its problems worse."},{"start":110.66,"end":113.5,"text":"Risk is the possibility that an investment loses value."},{"start":114.16,"end":120.66,"text":"Share prices can fall because profit falls, debt rises, competition grows, or the economy weakens."},{"start":121.46,"end":125.44,"text":"Toyota depends partly on demand for vehicles and the cost of making them."},{"start":126.2,"end":129.86,"text":"ASML depends partly on chipmakers ordering its machines."},{"start":130.94,"end":134.44,"text":"A real company can be strong today and still face future risk."},{"start":135.3,"end":138.46,"text":"Some companies share part of their profits directly with shareholders."},{"start":139.48,"end":140.94,"text":"These payments are called dividends."},{"start":141.6,"end":146.96,"text":"The payment schedule differs by company, and a company may raise, reduce, or stop its dividend."},{"start":147.84,"end":153.62,"text":"A dividend is normally calculated per share, so an owner with more shares receives more money."},{"start":154.4,"end":158.22,"text":"Microsoft reports both dividend payments and continued investment in its business."},{"start":159.12,"end":164.06,"text":"Other companies may keep more profit to build factories, develop products, or repay debt."},{"start":164.74,"end":174.2,"text":"A dividend can provide cash even when a share price does not rise, but it does not make a stock safe: the share price can still fall by more than the dividend paid."},{"start":175.5,"end":179.66,"text":"The difference between an individual stock and an index fund is concentration."},{"start":180.52,"end":183.9,"text":"An individual stock gives you ownership in one company."},{"start":184.52,"end":188.3,"text":"If that company does poorly, your investment can fall sharply."},{"start":189.06,"end":194.96,"text":"An index fund holds shares in many companies at once, so your money is spread across the companies it tracks."},{"start":195.58,"end":199.04,"text":"The S&P 500 covers 500 large U.S."},{"start":199.04,"end":207.12,"text":"companies, including Microsoft, and State Street's SPY ETF aims to follow that index before expenses."},{"start":207.68,"end":215.8,"text":"A TOPIX index fund follows a market-capitalization-weighted benchmark covering an extensive part of the Japanese stock market, including Toyota."},{"start":216.64,"end":225.98,"text":"A STOXX Europe 600 index fund follows 600 large, mid-sized, and small companies from 17 European countries, including ASML."},{"start":227.06,"end":233.36,"text":"Each regional index fund spreads company-specific risk, but it can still fall when its whole market falls."},{"start":233.94,"end":240.12,"text":"Diversification means spreading investments across different companies, industries, and countries to reduce risk."},{"start":240.96,"end":247.74,"text":"If a portfolio contains only car companies and the car industry struggles, its investments may fall together."},{"start":248.56,"end":257.3,"text":"If it also holds technology, healthcare, and companies from different countries, a fall in one area may have less effect on the whole portfolio."},{"start":258.26,"end":268.62,"text":"For example, Toyota operates in Japan's automotive industry, ASML is a Dutch maker of semiconductor equipment, and Microsoft is a U.S."},{"start":268.62,"end":270.08,"text":"software and cloud company."},{"start":271.22,"end":278.64,"text":"Holding these three stocks is more diversified than holding only one, but three stocks are still a small portfolio."},{"start":279.53,"end":282.5,"text":"A broad index fund can hold hundreds of companies."},{"start":284.08,"end":286.94,"text":"Diversification does not remove all risk."},{"start":287.5,"end":294.06,"text":"Many markets can fall at the same time, and a fund focused on one region is not the same as a global fund."},{"start":295.58,"end":300.8,"text":"Diversification mainly reduces the damage that one company or one industry can cause."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"share","start":0.18,"end":0.42},{"text":"is","start":0.42,"end":0.7},{"text":"one","start":0.7,"end":1.04},{"text":"unit","start":1.04,"end":1.4},{"text":"of","start":1.4,"end":1.64},{"text":"ownership","start":1.64,"end":2.04},{"text":"in","start":2.04,"end":2.38},{"text":"a","start":2.38,"end":2.5},{"text":"company","start":2.5,"end":2.88},{"text":"When","start":3.72,"end":3.86},{"text":"a","start":3.86,"end":4},{"text":"company","start":4,"end":4.26},{"text":"sells","start":4.26,"end":4.68},{"text":"shares","start":4.68,"end":5.08},{"text":"on","start":5.08,"end":5.34},{"text":"a","start":5.34,"end":5.44},{"text":"stock","start":5.44,"end":5.68},{"text":"exchange","start":5.68,"end":6.26},{"text":"anyone","start":6.66,"end":6.82},{"text":"can","start":6.82,"end":7.16},{"text":"buy","start":7.16,"end":7.36},{"text":"them","start":7.36,"end":7.6},{"text":"If","start":8.06,"end":8.16},{"text":"the","start":8.16,"end":8.3},{"text":"company","start":8.3,"end":8.56},{"text":"has","start":8.56,"end":8.84},{"text":"one","start":8.84,"end":9.14},{"text":"million","start":9.14,"end":9.46},{"text":"shares","start":9.46,"end":9.9},{"text":"and","start":9.9,"end":10.22},{"text":"you","start":10.22,"end":10.34},{"text":"buy","start":10.34,"end":10.52},{"text":"one","start":10.52,"end":11.11},{"text":"thousand","start":11.11,"end":11.7},{"text":"you","start":11.7,"end":11.84},{"text":"own","start":11.84,"end":12.0